  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-better-sidebar-lite)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-better-sidebar-lite)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-better-sidebar-lite.svg)\n**🌐 語言 / Language:** [English](./README.md) · [繁體中文](./README.zh-TW.md) · [Tiếng Việt](./README.vi.md)\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n  <img width=\"400\" height=\"400\" alt=\"review_1\" src=\"./printshots/avatar.png\" />\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": ";TLDR",
      "text": "Add a sidebar to the right side of the workspace screen with usefull tabs:\n- Explorer\n- Git\n- Skills\n- Tools"
    },
    {
      "section": "How to install",
      "text": "```\ndsh plugin add dsh-better-sidebar-lite@1.0.0-rs.1 --profile web\n```\n\n⚠️ **WARNING:** Make sure to install Deepseek Harness version 0.1.0-rc.7 or higher..."
    },
    {
      "section": "What is does ? (1.0.0-rs.1)",
      "text": "Add a sidebar to the right side of the workspace screen. This area will contain tabs displaying various pieces of information, including:\n- **Dock**: A right-docked sidebar occupying the frame's right details column, with native drag resize. Open/close it with the `Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+B` shortcut or the toggle button in the left sidebar footer; your open/closed preference is persisted.\n- **Editor**: Modal editors support viewing the content of objects — a file viewer (raw content or unified-diff side-by-side view) and a tool-detail card, rendered over the whole sidebar.\n- **Explorer**: \n  - Display the workspace folder tree, with directories lazy-loaded on demand.\n  - Open any file in the modal editor by double-clicking or pressing `Enter`.\n  - Full keyboard navigation: arrow keys, `Home`/`End`, `Enter`/`Space`, and `*` to expand one level.\n  - Automatically track changes in the workspace (stamp polling + session-dirty debounce), with a manual refresh and empty/error states (no workspace, deleted root, load failure).\n- **Git**:\n  - Status view with four sections — Staged, Conflicts, Changes, Untracked — each with counts.\n  - Stage/unstage per row, discard changes per file or discard all"
    },
    {
      "section": "The author's vision and future direction.",
      "text": "- Develop additional suitable features while maintaining the original philosophy of \"simplicity and effectiveness\".\n- Share additional plugins, system prompts, and other skills suitable for the Deepseek Harness system.\n- Support and contribute to the Deepseek Harness community.\n- Complete the challenge set for myself: 365 days (and beyond) of partnership with Deepseek Harness."
    },
    {
